# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scientific data, model artifacts, generated banks
# Never commit binary data — it bloats the repo and breaks `git clone`.
# Use external storage (HuggingFace Hub, S3, PhysioNet) instead.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.npy
*.npz
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.engine
*.tflite
*.ckpt
*.safetensors

# Root-anchored on purpose (CL-099). Without the leading slash these match at ANY
# depth, so a source package named src/myocard_egm_studio/data/ (or artifacts/, out/,
# ...) would be silently untracked — green locally, ModuleNotFoundError in CI. That
# is exactly how egm-classifier went red at Refactor Step 8.
/data/
/banks/
/checkpoints/
/runs/
/logs/
/mlruns/
/wandb/
/artifacts/

# `out/` is the exception to the anchoring above: it must match at ANY depth, because
# every shipped example spec writes a *relative* `out/...` path, so running one from
# examples/ produces examples/out/. The negation keeps CL-099's landmine defused — a
# source package src/<pkg>/out/ stays tracked. Verified both ways with git check-ignore.
out/
!src/**/out/

tests/charts/baseline

# Allow tiny fixtures committed under tests/fixtures/ if needed:
!tests/fixtures/**

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build / docs
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/_build/
site/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local dev-only tools (never committed; deleted once the GUI hosts them)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
examples/pyqtgraph_demo.py
